{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 510 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D5"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the hydromorphone hydrochloride shortage on 2017-10-31 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E38", "D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our injection supply (NDC 00409128331) is labeled by Hospira, Inc. from plants FEI 1021343 and FEI 1925262.",
      "cites": ["E18", "E30"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 976095 at FEI 1925262 ended 2016-06-08 and was classified OAI, 510 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D5", "E24"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to FEI 1925262 on 2017-02-14, 259 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E29"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1064827 at FEI 1925262 ended 2018-08-15 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2020-04-22.",
      "cites": ["D9", "E26"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked action is to transfer 173 units from Corvale General (21 days on hand) to Corvale East (9.5 days on hand), which would bring Corvale East to 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D11", "D1", "D2"]
    }
  ]
}
